# Copy to .env and fill in (.env is gitignored). config/settings.py (pydantic-settings) is the
# single reader; add a line here the moment a new var is introduced.

# --- Environment (ADR-0015) ---
# DECODE_ENV selects WHERE Settings gets its values, and nothing else:
#   local (default) → this .env file. Kitaru is never imported.
#   dev|staging|prod → the Environment Bucket, the DERIVED Kitaru secret `decode-<env>` (no override
#                      knob). This file is then DROPPED from the chain entirely, so a key missing from
#                      the bucket fails loudly at startup instead of being backfilled from here.
# Precedence is always: process env > (.env | bucket) > defaults.
# Mirror this file into a bucket with:  make sync-secrets ENV=<env>   (one-way; the file is the truth)
# DECODE_ENV=local
#
# CLEAN BREAK (ADR-0015 §4): RUNTIME_SECRET_NAME / RUNTIME_SECRET_STORE_CONFIG /
# RUNTIME_SECRET_STORE_MODEL_KEY are DELETED. No shim, no warning — a stale entry in your .env is
# now SILENTLY IGNORED. DECODE_ENV replaces all three (see CREDENTIALS.md).

# --- Inference: LLM provider ---
# One selectable provider; unset stays on gemini. Each has a free path (see README).
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini / openrouter / modal

GEMINI_API_KEY=changeme
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=changeme
# Default is the Free Models Router (auto-routes across free tool-capable models).
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free

# modal: your own endpoint — see MODAL_MODELS.md. Two DISTINCT credential pairs:
# (1) ACCOUNT tokens (MODAL_TOKEN_ID / MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET) — authenticate the modal CLI + the modal
#     sandbox. NOT settings, so putting them in this file does NOTHING: cli.py resolves them from the
#     PROCESS ENV exactly as the modal CLI does. Run `modal token set` (writes ~/.modal.toml), or
#     export both in your shell.
# (2) ENDPOINT vars — how decode calls the served model (base_url = {url}/v1):
# MODAL_ENDPOINT_URL=https://your-workspace--your-app.modal.run
# MODAL_ENDPOINT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8
# Proxy tokens from `modal workspace proxy-tokens create` — set both, or omit both (--unauthenticated):
# MODAL_PROXY_TOKEN_ID=wk-...
# MODAL_PROXY_TOKEN_SECRET=ws-...

# --- Logging ---
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# File-only logging, at .decode/logs/decode.log. The log-path override is NOT a setting: EXPORT it
# (logging.py reads the process env at import, before settings exist), e.g.
#   export DECODE_LOG_FILE=/tmp/decode.log   — and an empty string ("") disables file logging.

# --- Tool execution / output truncation ---
# BASH_TIMEOUT_S=120.0
# MAX_OUTPUT_LINES=2000                   # tool-output truncation caps (lines first, then bytes)
# MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES=50000
# WEB_FETCH_TIMEOUT_S=30.0

# --- Observability: Opik (ADR-0014) ---
# Presence-based: set OPIK_API_KEY (free at comet.com) to trace every turn/run; unset = byte-identical
# no-op. Keep this block commented so copying this file never enables tracing with a bogus key.
# OPIK_API_KEY=changeme
# OPIK_WORKSPACE=default
# The Opik project a trace is filed under. Defaults to decode-<DECODE_ENV> (local → decode-local,
# prod → decode-prod), so traces self-sort per environment; set this to override that.
# OPIK_PROJECT_NAME=decode-local
# Self-hosted OTLP base (exporter appends /v1/traces); unset = Comet cloud.
# OPIK_URL_OVERRIDE=http://localhost:5173/api/v1/private/otel
# USD per MILLION tokens, for a PER-TOKEN model whose price the catalog does not know. Gemini and
# mainstream OpenRouter slugs are priced automatically; set these only for an OpenRouter model that
# reports no cost, using the rate from its OpenRouter page. NOT for MODAL: a self-hosted endpoint
# bills GPU-seconds, not tokens, so any per-token figure there is invented — leave these unset and
# read Modal's own billing. Unset (0.0) = "unknown", and decode reports no cost at all.
# LLM_COST_INPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=0.0
# LLM_COST_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=0.0

# --- Harness artifacts & sessions ---
# Everything decode writes lives under <launch cwd>/.decode (ADR-0012 §6).
# DECODE_DIR=.decode
# SESSIONS_DIR=.decode/sessions

# --- Memory (AGENTS.md / MEMORY.md) ---
# MEMORY_MAX_LINES=200                    # MEMORY.md caps; the on-exit compressor fires at the line cap
# MEMORY_MAX_BYTES=25000

# --- Context compaction (ADR-0006) ---
# COMPACTION_ENABLED=true                 # gates only the automatic cascade; /compact always works
# Your model's max INPUT window; also drives the TUI gauge. RESOLVED per run for the model that run
# actually uses (`decode run --model <id>` included), first hit wins:
#   1. this setting, if you set it       — you own the number, and it suppresses the probe entirely
#   2. a provider probe                  — modal/OpenAI-compatible: GET {url}/v1/models -> max_model_len
#                                          gemini:     models.get(model=…)  -> input_token_limit
#                                          openrouter: GET /api/v1/models   -> context_length
#   3. a static table                    — Gemini 2.5/3.5 -> 1048576, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B -> 262144
#   4. 200000                            — the conservative assumption, said once at startup
# The probe is best effort: it runs at most once per model per process, never on `--help`/`--version`,
# and any failure (offline, 401, timeout) silently falls through to the table. Set this to override —
# e.g. to your endpoint's max_model_len — or to skip the probe on a slow cold-starting endpoint.
# COMPACTION_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS=262144
# Tiers fire at window*(1-reserve): full at 80%, micro at 60% — keep micro's reserve larger.
# COMPACTION_RESERVE_FRACTION=0.20
# MICROCOMPACTION_RESERVE_FRACTION=0.40
# COMPACTION_KEEP_RECENT_TOKENS=20000     # verbatim recent tail kept by full compaction
# MEMORY_COMPRESSION_ENABLED=true         # on-exit MEMORY.md compressor (drop-oldest fallback)

# --- Orchestration ---
# SLEEP_MAX_S=60.0                        # cap on the ungated sleep tool

# --- Subagents (ADR-0013) ---
# SUBAGENT_MAX_PARALLEL=4                 # children at once (mind free-tier rate limits)
# SUBAGENT_MAX_REQUESTS=25                # per-child model-request cap
# SUBAGENT_RESULT_MAX_BYTES=16000         # cap on a child's report

# --- Permissions ---
# Optional allow/deny rules; missing/malformed is non-fatal.
# PERMISSIONS_FILE=.decode/settings.json

# --- Skills ---
# Project skills: <name>/SKILL.md dirs; frontmatter `name` overrides a same-named built-in.
# SKILLS_DIR=.decode/skills

# --- LSP / code intelligence (ADR-0007) ---
# Best-effort: an absent/slow server degrades silently.
# LSP_ENABLED=true                        # master gate; false = no server ever spawned
# LSP_SERVER_COMMAND=ty                   # spawn = [command, *args]; args is a JSON list
# LSP_SERVER_ARGS=["server"]
# LSP_DIAGNOSTICS_ON_EDIT=true            # passive post-edit enricher only
# LSP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S=10.0

# --- Kitaru durable runtime (ADR-0008) ---
# Headless `decode run`; at DECODE_ENV=local the REPL never imports Kitaru.
# RUNTIME_ENABLED=true
# RUNTIME_CHECKPOINT_STRATEGY=calls       # calls (replay-ready) | turn (coarse); HITL forces calls
# RUNTIME_WAIT_TIMEOUT_S=600.0            # durable HITL wait poll timeout
# Secrets are NOT a runtime knob any more — see the DECODE_ENV block at the top of this file.

# --- Sandboxing (ADR-0012) ---
# A sandbox mode moves the WHOLE tool scope (file tools + bash) into an isolated /workspace.
# Fresh-exec: the filesystem persists across calls, cd/export don't.
# SANDBOX_MODE=none                       # none (host, default) | docker (local bind mount) | modal (remote)
# SANDBOX_IMAGE=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:python3.12-bookworm-slim   # must include bash; git added per backend
# SANDBOX_WORKSPACE_DIR=.decode/sandbox   # the host dir that IS the workspace
# Repo cloned into the workspace (--repo overrides; --local = fast local clone). On exit / /ship a
# decode/<session-id> branch is pushed back HOST-SIDE — no credential ever enters the sandbox.
# SANDBOX_REPO=
# SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_S=600.0                 # modal sandbox lifetime
# SANDBOX_GIT_USER_NAME=decode            # in-workspace commit identity (credentials stay host-side)
# SANDBOX_GIT_USER_EMAIL=decode@localhost
# One token for in-sandbox git push/PR (ADR-0016 §2): BOTH backends inject it straight into the
# worker env as GITHUB_TOKEN (+ git's credential helper). A sandboxed process CAN read it — use a
# scoped, revocable PAT. Empty = hand-back only (host-side; no credential enters the sandbox).
# SANDBOX_GIT_TOKEN=

# --- Evals (ADR-0017) ---
# The eval suite lives in top-level evals/ (NOT shipped in the wheel) but reads these off the same
# Settings surface. Only exercised by `make eval-benchmark` / `make eval-regression` (+ `python -m evals
# online`), never `make ci`. The two make targets run the real agent AND store an Opik experiment;
# `online` instead grades traces decode ALREADY emitted, scored in the live project. All three need
# OPIK_API_KEY (above — to reach/store Opik) + the active provider's key so the judge can grade
# (LLM_PROVIDER: gemini -> GEMINI_API_KEY, openrouter -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY, modal -> MODAL_ENDPOINT_URL).
# Missing a key = skip friendly, exit 0. Full map of the four tracks: docs/evals.md.
# LiteLLM model string for the G-Eval / conversation judges; empty derives it from LLM_PROVIDER, so the
# judges follow decode's own provider.
# EVAL_JUDGE_MODEL=
# The Opik project eval runs log under — kept apart from the live-REPL project so eval and production
# traces never mix.
# EVAL_PROJECT_NAME=decode-evals
